{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01SuCMxg9CrGmkEwiVBngYJP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user wants me to generate detailed imagined experiment results for the \"worst\" tier across all planned experiments in the experiment_plan. Let me carefully go through each planned experiment and generate realistic worst-tier predictions with rationales.\n\nLet me review the worst tier definition:\n- C2 is disproven (binarized Likert is also significant) OR effects don't generalize\n- Key assumptions include things like binarized Likert sign test being significant, only GPT-4o showing significance, casual-original subset ~50%, exp-002 not replicating, formality main effect disappearing in logistic regression\n\n\n- Now I'm looking at the metric ranges I'll use to construct these worst-case scenarios, with binarized Likert p-values staying significant, pairwise comparisons showing minimal effects, and the logistic regression coefficients becoming non-significant for formality while original status remains robust.\n\n- I'm reviewing each planned experiment to identify the failure modes: the multi-judge and multi-benchmark approaches might not replicate across different conditions, the sensitivity analysis could show the effect is specific to certain model-benchmark combinations, the tone axis serves as a negative control, the pairwise rate control tests whether original preference dominates, and the scaled replication checks if the effect holds at larger sample sizes.\n\n- The remaining experiments test alternative hypotheses: whether different rewriter models produce the same results, whether binarized Likert scoring changes significance, how sensitive the findings are to NLI thresholds, whether the consistency filter introduces systematic bias, if human validation supports the NLI approach, and whether a formal statistical model reveals that formality isn't actually the driving factor.\n\n- Now I'm filtering down to just the planned experiments and preparing to structure them in YAML format.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13409,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13409},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"da4318c9-9c05-4345-960e-f3d28301a98e","uuid":"bc948c68-2d04-4d63-9669-144bc28030f6"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01SuCMxg9CrGmkEwiVBngYJP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  C2 (\"Likert Blindspot\") 被证伪或效应不泛化。binarized Likert sign test 显著 (p<0.04)\n  证明 Likert-Pairwise gap 来自统计检验功效差异而非测量方法结构性优势；或者效应仅限\n  GPT-4o × LLMBar，Claude/Gemini 均不显著，additional benchmarks 不复制。需要根本性\n  reframe：路径 A (sensitivity-specificity tradeoffs) 或路径 B (original-text preference\n  confound as cautionary negative result)。C4 在此 tier 反而更重要——\"what NOT to do\"\n  本身就是贡献。目标仍为 EMNLP Findings (projected 2.8-3.3)。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Multi-judge formality pairwise\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: >\n      在 Claude-3.5/4-Sonnet 和 Gemini-2.0-Flash 上复制 formality pairwise 实验。\n      使用已有 counterfactuals，dual-direction pairwise with position control。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_formal_win_rate: 0.691\n      gpt4o_sign_p: 0.006\n      claude_formal_win_rate: 0.545\n      claude_sign_p: 0.42\n      claude_n_consistent: 44\n      claude_formal_wins: 24\n      claude_casual_wins: 20\n      gemini_formal_win_rate: 0.52\n      gemini_sign_p: 0.68\n      gemini_n_consistent: 48\n      gemini_formal_wins: 25\n      gemini_casual_wins: 23\n      n_judges_pairwise_significant: 1\n      cross_judge_formal_win_rate: 0.552\n      cross_judge_pairwise_p_median: 0.42\n    result_rationale: >\n      worst 档核心假设之一：formality bias 是 GPT-4o-specific artifact 而非 universal\n      bias。Claude 和 Gemini 的 RLHF 训练数据和 reward model 不同，对 formality 的\n      偏好结构不同。GPT-4o 的 69.1% formal win rate 可能来自其特定的 instruction tuning\n      偏好（OpenAI 系模型已知偏好更 formal/structured 输出），而非 LLM judge 的通用\n      属性。Claude 略偏 formal (54.5%) 但远未达显著；Gemini 基本 50/50。这意味着\n      \"style bias in LLM judges\" 这个 universal claim 无法成立，只能说 \"GPT-4o\n      exhibits formality preference as a judge\"。cross_judge median p=0.42 远超 0.05。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 2: Multi-Judge Formality Pairwise Results\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"N_consistent\", \"Formal_wins\", \"Casual_wins\", \"Win_rate\", \"Sign_p\", \"Wilson_CI\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", 55, 38, 17, \"69.1%\", \"0.006**\", \"[0.56, 0.80]\"]\n          - [\"Claude-3.5-Sonnet\", 44, 24, 20, \"54.5%\", \"0.42\", \"[0.40, 0.69]\"]\n          - [\"Gemini-2.0-Flash\", 48, 25, 23, \"52.1%\", \"0.68\", \"[0.38, 0.66]\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot: 三个 judge 的 formal win rate 及 95% Wilson CI。GPT-4o CI 不含 50%，Claude 和 Gemini CI 宽且跨 50%。视觉上清晰显示效应不泛化。\"\n    analysis: >\n      仅 GPT-4o 显著。Fisher combined p 可能因 GPT-4o 的强信号勉强达 0.05 左右，\n      但 heterogeneity 极大 (I²>70%)。无法声称 \"LLM judges exhibit formality bias\"\n      — 只能说 \"GPT-4o as judge prefers formal text\"。这直接削弱 C1 的 generality\n      和论文的 impact scope。路径 B framing 下可以说 \"the bias we detect is\n      judge-specific, underscoring the need for multi-judge validation in bias audits\"。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      在 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench/Arena-Hard subsets 上运行 CSD pipeline。\n      新 counterfactual generation + 三个 judge 评估。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_formal_win_rate: 0.56\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_sign_p: 0.31\n      gpt4o_mtbench_formal_win_rate: 0.53\n      gpt4o_mtbench_sign_p: 0.55\n      claude_alpacaeval_formal_win_rate: 0.51\n      claude_alpacaeval_sign_p: 0.84\n      claude_mtbench_formal_win_rate: 0.48\n      claude_mtbench_sign_p: 0.72\n      gemini_alpacaeval_formal_win_rate: 0.50\n      gemini_alpacaeval_sign_p: 0.95\n      gemini_mtbench_formal_win_rate: 0.54\n      gemini_mtbench_sign_p: 0.49\n      n_benchmarks_with_gap: 0\n      nli_pass_rate_alpacaeval: 0.82\n      nli_pass_rate_mtbench: 0.79\n      n_combos_significant_of_6: 0\n    result_rationale: >\n      worst 档假设 exp-002 不复制 (p>0.15 across all new combos)。原因是多方面的：\n      (1) LLMBar 的 task 结构特殊——它是专门测试 judge 能力的 benchmark，response pairs\n      有明确的 correct/incorrect 之分，formality 在 \"明确有对错\" 的场景下更容易影响\n      judge 的边界决策；AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 的 response 质量差异更大更 noisy，\n      style bias 被 quality signal 淹没。(2) 不同 benchmark 的 source text 风格分布\n      不同——AlpacaEval 多为 instruction-following，本身已偏 formal；MT-Bench 更 diverse，\n      counterfactual rewriting 的质量可能不均匀。(3) NLI pass rate 略低 (79-82% vs\n      LLMBar 88%) 暗示 counterfactual quality 在 out-of-domain text 上有退化。\n      这意味着 GPT-4o × LLMBar 的发现是 benchmark-specific 而非 generalizable。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 3: Cross-Benchmark Formality Pairwise (3 judges × 3 benchmarks)\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"Benchmark\", \"N_consistent\", \"Formal_WR\", \"Sign_p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", \"LLMBar\", 55, \"69.1%\", \"0.006**\"]\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", \"AlpacaEval\", 48, \"56.3%\", \"0.31\"]\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", \"MT-Bench\", 42, \"52.4%\", \"0.55\"]\n          - [\"Claude\", \"LLMBar\", 44, \"54.5%\", \"0.42\"]\n          - [\"Claude\", \"AlpacaEval\", 45, \"51.1%\", \"0.84\"]\n          - [\"Claude\", \"MT-Bench\", 40, \"47.5%\", \"0.72\"]\n          - [\"Gemini\", \"LLMBar\", 48, \"52.1%\", \"0.68\"]\n          - [\"Gemini\", \"AlpacaEval\", 46, \"50.0%\", \"0.95\"]\n          - [\"Gemini\", \"MT-Bench\", 43, \"53.5%\", \"0.49\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap: 3×3 judge×benchmark 的 formal win rate，颜色编码偏离 50% 程度。仅左上角 (GPT-4o × LLMBar) 显著着色，其余接近中性灰。\"\n    analysis: >\n      9 个 judge×benchmark 组合中仅 1 个显著 (GPT-4o × LLMBar)，Bonferroni 校正后\n      连这一个也不再显著 (0.006 × 9 = 0.054)。这是 worst 档最致命的发现——如果\n      formality bias 仅在特定 judge × benchmark 交叉处出现，则无法支撑任何 general\n      claim。路径 B 下可 reframe 为 \"benchmark characteristics mediate bias\n      detectability\"，但说服力有限。\n\n  - name: \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      对每个 judge × benchmark 组合，同时计算 Likert ATE 和 pairwise win rate，\n      系统比较测量敏感度。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_llmbar_likert_ate: -0.102\n      gpt4o_llmbar_likert_p: 0.33\n      gpt4o_llmbar_pairwise_wr: 0.691\n      gpt4o_llmbar_pairwise_p: 0.006\n      gpt4o_llmbar_gap: \"significant\"\n      claude_llmbar_likert_ate: 0.05\n      claude_llmbar_likert_p: 0.61\n      claude_llmbar_pairwise_wr: 0.545\n      claude_llmbar_pairwise_p: 0.42\n      claude_llmbar_gap: \"neither significant\"\n      gemini_llmbar_likert_ate: 0.02\n      gemini_llmbar_likert_p: 0.82\n      gemini_llmbar_pairwise_wr: 0.521\n      gemini_llmbar_pairwise_p: 0.68\n      gemini_llmbar_gap: \"neither significant\"\n      n_combos_with_likert_pairwise_gap: 1\n      n_combos_both_null: 7\n      n_combos_pairwise_only_significant: 1\n    result_rationale: >\n      worst 档下 Likert-Pairwise gap 仅在 GPT-4o × LLMBar 出现——这正是已知数据点。\n      其他 8 个组合中，pairwise 和 Likert 都不显著，所以 \"gap\" 无从谈起。这使得 C2\n      (\"Likert Blindspot\") 的证据基础极度单薄：唯一的 gap 案例可能是 statistical\n      fluke 或 GPT-4o 特有的评分模式。更关键的是，当 exp-010 binarized Likert 也\n      显著时，连这唯一的 gap 也被解释为统计检验差异而非测量方法差异。C2 作为主贡献\n      完全瓦解。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 4: Likert vs Pairwise Sensitivity Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"Benchmark\", \"Likert_ATE\", \"Likert_p\", \"Pairwise_WR\", \"Pairwise_p\", \"Gap\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", \"LLMBar\", \"-0.10\", \"0.33\", \"69.1%\", \"0.006**\", \"Pairwise-only\"]\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", \"AlpacaEval\", \"0.04\", \"0.71\", \"56.3%\", \"0.31\", \"Neither\"]\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", \"MT-Bench\", \"0.01\", \"0.92\", \"52.4%\", \"0.55\", \"Neither\"]\n          - [\"Claude\", \"LLMBar\", \"0.05\", \"0.61\", \"54.5%\", \"0.42\", \"Neither\"]\n          - [\"Claude\", \"AlpacaEval\", \"-0.02\", \"0.85\", \"51.1%\", \"0.84\", \"Neither\"]\n          - [\"Claude\", \"MT-Bench\", \"0.03\", \"0.77\", \"47.5%\", \"0.72\", \"Neither\"]\n          - [\"Gemini\", \"LLMBar\", \"0.02\", \"0.82\", \"52.1%\", \"0.68\", \"Neither\"]\n          - [\"Gemini\", \"AlpacaEval\", \"0.00\", \"0.99\", \"50.0%\", \"0.95\", \"Neither\"]\n          - [\"Gemini\", \"MT-Bench\", \"0.06\", \"0.55\", \"53.5%\", \"0.49\", \"Neither\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired bar chart: 每个 judge×benchmark 组合的 Likert p-value vs Pairwise p-value，红线标 0.05。仅一个组合的 pairwise 柱低于红线。\"\n    analysis: >\n      C2 的 \"Likert Blindspot\" narrative 需要在多个条件下观察到 Likert fails but\n      pairwise detects 的模式。worst 档下仅 1/9 出现此模式，且该唯一案例即将被\n      exp-010 解释为统计检验差异。Likert 和 pairwise 在 8/9 条件下一致报告无效应——\n      这更像 \"there is no bias to detect\" 而非 \"Likert misses bias\"。\n\n  - name: \"Tone axis negative control\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-004\"\n    description: >\n      Tone pilot 已失败 (NLI 65%, joint gate 45%)。作为 negative control 记录\n      epistemic commitment 改变与 NLI verification 的结构性不兼容。\n    expected_results:\n      nli_cf_pass_rate: 0.65\n      both_pass_rate: 0.45\n      failure_mode: \"epistemic commitment change\"\n      role_in_paper: \"negative control — axis boundary evidence\"\n      assertive_nli_mean: 0.656\n      hedging_nli_mean: 0.793\n      catastrophic_nli_failures: 6\n    result_rationale: >\n      此实验无论 tier 结果不变——tone 的 pilot 数据已确定失败。worst 档下 tone\n      作为 negative control 的价值不变，但 C3 (axis 依赖性) 的支撑变弱：\n      working axis 只有 formality 一个（verbosity 也失败了），而 formality 又只在\n      GPT-4o × LLMBar 上显著。\"one working axis on one judge on one benchmark\"\n      不足以支撑任何关于 axis 语义性质的 claim。在路径 A/B reframe 中，tone 仅\n      作为方法论 boundary 的 footnote。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Method boundary diagram: formality (content-preserving ✅) vs tone (epistemic commitment change ✗) vs verbosity (information-changing ✗)。简单分类图，不需要新数据。\"\n    analysis: >\n      C3 在 worst 档下降级为 \"we tested three axes, only one worked on one judge\"，\n      贡献极有限。路径 B 下可以说 \"counterfactual approach has narrow applicability\n      window\"，但这本身不是正面贡献。\n\n  - name: \"Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      Pairwise 比较 original text 与其 RATE double-rewrite (same style)，量化\n      original preference confound。扩展到所有 judge × benchmark 组合。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_llmbar_orig_pref_wr: 0.62\n      gpt4o_llmbar_orig_pref_p: 0.048\n      claude_llmbar_orig_pref_wr: 0.58\n      claude_llmbar_orig_pref_p: 0.18\n      gemini_llmbar_orig_pref_wr: 0.56\n      gemini_llmbar_orig_pref_p: 0.31\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_orig_pref_wr: 0.59\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_orig_pref_p: 0.12\n      gpt4o_mtbench_orig_pref_wr: 0.61\n      gpt4o_mtbench_orig_pref_p: 0.06\n      cross_condition_orig_pref_mean: 0.59\n      casual_orig_formal_win_rate_gpt4o: 0.545\n      casual_orig_formal_win_rate_claude: 0.50\n      casual_orig_formal_win_rate_gemini: 0.48\n      casual_orig_formal_win_rate_best_judge: 0.545\n    result_rationale: >\n      worst 档核心假设：original preference 解释了大部分甚至全部观测到的 \"style bias\"。\n      GPT-4o 的 formal win rate 69.1% 中，original preference 贡献 ~12pp（原文偏好\n      62%），剩余 formality 特异效应仅 ~7pp。更关键的是 casual-original subset：\n      当 original 是 casual（即 formal version 是 rewrite），formal win rate 仅\n      54.5%——接近 50%，说明一旦去除 original preference，formality bias 几乎消失。\n      GPT-4o × LLMBar 的 dir_casual_orig_win_rate 已有数据 (0.5455, p=0.83)，\n      在 worst 档下这个模式跨 judge 和 benchmark 持续：所有 casual-original subset\n      的 formal win rate 在 45-54% 之间。这意味着 \"formality bias\" 可能本质上是\n      \"original text preference + directional confound\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 5: Original Preference Confound (RATE Control)\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"Benchmark\", \"Orig_pref_WR\", \"Orig_pref_p\", \"Casual-orig_formal_WR\", \"Casual-orig_p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", \"LLMBar\", \"62.0%\", \"0.048*\", \"54.5%\", \"0.83\"]\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", \"AlpacaEval\", \"59.0%\", \"0.12\", \"51.2%\", \"0.91\"]\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", \"MT-Bench\", \"61.0%\", \"0.06\", \"50.0%\", \"1.00\"]\n          - [\"Claude\", \"LLMBar\", \"58.0%\", \"0.18\", \"50.0%\", \"1.00\"]\n          - [\"Gemini\", \"LLMBar\", \"56.0%\", \"0.31\", \"48.0%\", \"0.72\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Decomposition bar chart: 每个 judge×benchmark 的 formal win rate 分解为 original preference component + residual formality component。视觉上显示 residual 接近 0。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Original preference 是 ubiquitous confound (跨 judge 56-62%)，而 residual\n      formality effect 在控制后接近 0。这是路径 B 的核心证据：\"apparent style bias\n      is confounded with original-text preference\"。casual-original subset 的 ~50%\n      win rate 是最干净的证据——当 formality 和 original preference 方向相反时，\n      formality bias 消失。\n\n  - name: \"Scaled replication (n=300-500)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      将 GPT-4o × LLMBar formality 实验从 n=100 扩展到 n=300-500。\n      Power analysis 确定 minimum detectable effect size。\n    expected_results:\n      n_total: 400\n      n_valid_consistent: 220\n      formal_wins: 132\n      casual_wins: 88\n      formal_win_rate: 0.60\n      sign_p: 0.004\n      wilson_ci: [0.534, 0.663]\n      power_at_d02: 0.35\n      power_at_d05: 0.88\n      casual_orig_subset_n: 95\n      casual_orig_formal_wr: 0.516\n      casual_orig_p: 0.67\n      nli_pass_rate: 0.85\n      effect_size_cohens_h: 0.20\n    result_rationale: >\n      worst 档下扩大样本量反而暴露了效应的脆弱性。overall formal win rate 从 69.1%\n      下降到 60.0%——n=100 的高 win rate 部分是小样本 noise。更重要的是，casual-original\n      subset 在 n≈95 时 formal win rate 仅 51.6% (p=0.67)，证实 formality 效应在\n      控制 original preference 后消失。effect size (Cohen's h=0.20) 属于 small，\n      且 power analysis 显示在 d=0.02 (trivial effect) 下 power 仅 35%——如果真实\n      效应是 trivial 的，n=400 也检测不到。overall p=0.004 仍显著，但这混淆了\n      formality 和 original preference。路径 B 下这是核心数据：\"at scale, the\n      significant overall effect decomposes into original preference + noise\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 6: Scaled Replication Results (n=400)\"\n        columns: [\"Subset\", \"N\", \"Formal_WR\", \"Sign_p\", \"95% CI\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"All consistent\", 220, \"60.0%\", \"0.004**\", \"[0.534, 0.663]\"]\n          - [\"Formal-original\", 125, \"66.4%\", \"0.001**\", \"[0.577, 0.742]\"]\n          - [\"Casual-original\", 95, \"51.6%\", \"0.67\", \"[0.415, 0.615]\"]\n          - [\"NLI≥0.90\", 187, \"61.5%\", \"0.003**\", \"[0.543, 0.683]\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Formal win rate 随 n 增长的 running average plot，标 95% CI band。显示效应从 ~69% 向 ~60% 收敛，且 casual-original subset 收敛到 ~50%。\"\n    analysis: >\n      n=400 确认了两个关键 worst 档特征：(1) 整体效应存在但 attenuated (60% vs 69%)；\n      (2) casual-original subset 效应消失。这支持路径 B 的 \"original preference\n      confound\" 解释。签发 p<0.01 但科学意义需要 decomposition。\n\n  - name: \"Register axis (academic/conversational)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: >\n      第三个 surface-level axis 测试。Academic vs conversational register 改变\n      词汇和句式但不改变信息内容。\n    expected_results:\n      n: 100\n      nli_pass_rate: 0.72\n      bertscore_pass_rate: 0.58\n      joint_pass_rate: 0.48\n      stopped_at: \"content_verification\"\n      stop_reason: \"NLI 72% < 80% threshold\"\n      academic_to_conversational_nli_mean: 0.81\n      conversational_to_academic_nli_mean: 0.65\n    result_rationale: >\n      worst 档下 register 也在 content verification 阶段失败。原因：academic→conversational\n      转换不可避免地涉及 precision 和 hedging 的变化——学术 register 的 \"our findings\n      demonstrate\" 变成口语 \"we found\" 时，NLI 可能 pass；但学术 register 的\n      \"statistically significant correlation (r=0.82, p<0.001)\" 变成口语 \"there's\n      a pretty strong link\" 时，NLI 正确地检测到信息损失。conversational→academic\n      方向更差 (NLI 65%) 因为 academic register 要求添加精确性（hedging qualifiers,\n      citations 等），这改变了认知承诺。72% 总通过率低于 80% 阈值。这意味着 CSD\n      方法仅对 formality 这一个 axis 有效——方法的适用范围极窄。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table A3: Register Axis Content Verification\"\n        columns: [\"Direction\", \"N\", \"NLI_mean\", \"NLI≥0.80\", \"BERTScore_mean\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Academic→Conversational\", 52, \"0.81\", \"73%\", \"0.82\"]\n          - [\"Conversational→Academic\", 48, \"0.65\", \"52%\", \"0.77\"]\n          - [\"Overall\", 100, \"0.72\", \"63%\", \"0.80\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      register 加入 tone 和 verbosity 成为第三个失败的 axis。CSD 方法的适用范围\n      收窄到仅 formality——且即使 formality 也仅在 GPT-4o × LLMBar 上显著。\n      C3 完全不成立。路径 A/B 下 C3 最多降级为 footnote：\"we attempted three additional\n      axes; all failed content verification, establishing narrow applicability\"。\n\n  - name: \"Non-Qwen rewriter control\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      使用 Llama-3.1-70B 作为 rewriter 替代 Qwen3-32B，排除 Qwen-family artifacts。\n    expected_results:\n      llama_nli_pass_rate: 0.80\n      llama_bertscore_mean: 0.88\n      llama_formal_win_rate_gpt4o: 0.58\n      llama_sign_p: 0.21\n      qwen_formal_win_rate_gpt4o: 0.691\n      qwen_sign_p: 0.006\n      rewriter_agreement_on_direction: 0.72\n      nli_correlation_qwen_llama: 0.61\n    result_rationale: >\n      worst 档下 Llama rewriter 产生不同结果：formal win rate 从 69.1% 降到 58%\n      (p=0.21, 不显著)。这不一定意味着 Qwen 有 artifact——Llama 和 Qwen 的 rewriting\n      style 不同，Llama 可能在 formalization 时引入更多 content changes (NLI 80%\n      vs Qwen 88%)。但 worst 档的解读是：结果对 rewriter choice 敏感，且仅 Qwen 版本\n      显著。这引入 \"researcher degrees of freedom\" 质疑——如果换一个 rewriter 就不\n      显著了，结论有多 robust？审稿人会 flag this。NLI correlation 0.61 说明两个\n      rewriter 的 counterfactuals 在内容保持度上有系统性差异。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table A4: Rewriter Robustness Check\"\n        columns: [\"Rewriter\", \"NLI_pass\", \"Formal_WR\", \"Sign_p\", \"N_consistent\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Qwen3-32B\", \"88%\", \"69.1%\", \"0.006**\", 55]\n          - [\"Llama-3.1-70B\", \"80%\", \"58.0%\", \"0.21\", 50]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot: 100 pairs 的 Qwen NLI score vs Llama NLI score，标 0.80 threshold 线。显示 moderate correlation 但有 substantial disagreement zone。\"\n    analysis: >\n      rewriter sensitivity 在 worst 档下是额外的 credibility hit。如果声称检测到\n      formality bias，但另一个 rewriter 检测不到，审稿人有理由质疑方法的可靠性。\n      路径 B 下可以 acknowledge 为 methodology caveat。\n\n  - name: \"Binarized Likert sign test (C2 critical control)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-010\"\n    description: >\n      对已有 scored_32b.jsonl 数据做 binarized Likert sign test：对每对样本，\n      formal version Likert 分数严格高于 casual version 的次数。如果显著 → C2 证伪。\n    expected_results:\n      n_pairs: 88\n      formal_higher: 42\n      casual_higher: 26\n      tied: 20\n      n_non_tied: 68\n      binarized_sign_p: 0.032\n      formal_higher_rate: 0.618\n      effect_direction: \"formal preferred in binarized Likert too\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      这是 worst 档对 C2 的致命打击。binarized Likert sign test p=0.032 < 0.04，\n      说明 Likert 数据本身就包含 formality preference 信号——paired t-test p=0.33\n      不显著是因为 Likert 评分的连续值方差太大（评分是 1-5 粗粒度，配对差异 noise\n      大），而非 Likert 作为测量方法看不到 bias。换言之，Likert-Pairwise gap 来自\n      sign test vs paired t-test 的统计功效差异：sign test 只看方向不看幅度，对\n      小而一致的偏好更敏感；paired t-test 受幅度方差影响更大。这意味着 \"Likert\n      Blindspot\" 这个 framing 完全错误——不是 Likert 看不到，而是配对 t 检验在\n      粗粒度评分上功效不足。任何使用 sign test 的方法（无论 Likert 还是 pairwise）\n      都能检测到效应。C2 从 \"measurement method structural advantage\" 坍缩为\n      \"statistical test choice matters\"——这是 trivially true 且 novelty 极低。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 7: Binarized Likert vs Pairwise Sign Test Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"N_non-tied\", \"Formal_preferred\", \"Preferred_rate\", \"Sign_test_p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Likert (paired t-test)\", 88, \"—\", \"—\", \"0.332\"]\n          - [\"Likert (binarized sign test)\", 68, 42, \"61.8%\", \"0.032*\"]\n          - [\"Pairwise (sign test)\", 55, 38, \"69.1%\", \"0.006**\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"三栏对比图：左=Likert paired t-test (NS)，中=Binarized Likert sign test (p=0.032)，右=Pairwise sign test (p=0.006)。视觉化显示 gap 来自 test choice 而非 measurement method。\"\n    analysis: >\n      C2 证伪。\"Likert Blindspot\" framing 不成立。路径 A 的 reframe 方向是：\n      \"Pairwise comparison amplifies weak bias signals through rank-based aggregation,\n      but this amplification also inflates false positive risk。Likert and pairwise\n      should be treated as complementary detectors with different sensitivity-specificity\n      tradeoffs。\" 标题改为 \"Sensitivity-Specificity Tradeoffs in LLM Judge Bias\n      Detection\"。C2 变为 descriptive (\"不同方法有不同检测特性\") 而非 prescriptive\n      (\"用 pairwise 替代 Likert\")。\n\n  - name: \"NLI threshold sensitivity analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-011\"\n    description: >\n      测试 NLI threshold 从 70% 到 95% 对结果的影响。零成本 reanalysis。\n    expected_results:\n      threshold_70_n: 82\n      threshold_70_formal_wr: 0.65\n      threshold_70_p: 0.018\n      threshold_75_n: 75\n      threshold_75_formal_wr: 0.67\n      threshold_75_p: 0.012\n      threshold_80_n: 68\n      threshold_80_formal_wr: 0.68\n      threshold_80_p: 0.009\n      threshold_85_n: 58\n      threshold_85_formal_wr: 0.70\n      threshold_85_p: 0.006\n      threshold_90_n: 46\n      threshold_90_formal_wr: 0.74\n      threshold_90_p: 0.002\n      threshold_95_n: 30\n      threshold_95_formal_wr: 0.77\n      threshold_95_p: 0.005\n      monotonic_increase: true\n      critical_finding: \"higher threshold → higher effect size but smaller n\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      结果单调递增：NLI threshold 越高，formal win rate 越高。worst 档的解读不是\n      \"方法 robust\"，而是 \"NLI threshold 与 effect size 正相关暗示 content quality\n      是 confound\"。高 NLI 的 pairs 是 rewriting 质量最好的——它们的 formal version\n      更 polished（因为高质量 rewriting 既保持内容又提升文风），所以 judge 偏好 formal\n      version 可能反映的是 rewriting quality 而非 formality bias。在 threshold 70%\n      时效应较弱 (65%, p=0.018)，95% 时最强 (77%, p=0.005)——但 n 从 82 降到 30。\n      这个 tradeoff 本身不致命，但 worst 档下审稿人会质疑：高 NLI pairs 是否\n      systematically 不同于低 NLI pairs？\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table A5: NLI Threshold Sensitivity\"\n        columns: [\"Threshold\", \"N_consistent\", \"Formal_WR\", \"Sign_p\", \"Cohen's_h\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"0.70\", 60, \"65.0%\", \"0.018\", \"0.31\"]\n          - [\"0.75\", 56, \"67.0%\", \"0.012\", \"0.35\"]\n          - [\"0.80\", 52, \"68.0%\", \"0.009\", \"0.37\"]\n          - [\"0.85\", 46, \"70.0%\", \"0.006\", \"0.41\"]\n          - [\"0.90\", 38, \"73.7%\", \"0.002\", \"0.49\"]\n          - [\"0.95\", 26, \"76.9%\", \"0.005\", \"0.57\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Dual-axis line chart: x=NLI threshold, left y=formal win rate (上升), right y=n (下降)。显示 sensitivity-sample size tradeoff。\"\n    analysis: >\n      结果 technically robust（所有 threshold 下均显著），但 worst 档的叙事不需要\n      这个实验不显著——它需要的是 effect size 与 threshold 的正相关暗示 confound。\n      路径 B 下这可以作为 \"methodological caveat: NLI filtering may introduce\n      selection bias toward higher-quality rewrites\"。\n\n  - name: \"Consistency filter bias analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-012\"\n    description: >\n      比较 position-consistent vs inconsistent pairs 的 NLI scores, text lengths,\n      task types。零成本 reanalysis。\n    expected_results:\n      consistent_n: 55\n      inconsistent_n: 43\n      discard_rate: 0.439\n      consistent_mean_nli: 0.91\n      inconsistent_mean_nli: 0.87\n      nli_diff_p: 0.08\n      consistent_mean_orig_len: 285\n      inconsistent_mean_orig_len: 342\n      length_diff_p: 0.03\n      consistent_formal_longer_pct: 0.58\n      inconsistent_formal_longer_pct: 0.51\n      task_type_distribution_differs: true\n      chi2_task_type_p: 0.04\n    result_rationale: >\n      worst 档下 consistency filter 引入了系统性偏差。consistent pairs (55/98) 相比\n      inconsistent pairs 有：(1) 更高的 NLI scores (0.91 vs 0.87, p=0.08, marginal)；\n      (2) 更短的原文 (285 vs 342 chars, p=0.03, 显著)；(3) formal version 更常更长\n      (58% vs 51%)。更关键的是 task type 分布不同 (χ²p=0.04)——consistent pairs\n      过度代表了某些 task types。这意味着 42-52% 的丢弃率不是随机的，retained pairs\n      是一个 biased subsample。审稿人可以合理质疑：观测到的 formality bias 是否\n      仅反映了 filter 保留的特定 task types 的特征？如果 shorter texts 更容易被\n      formality 影响（因为 style 在 content 中的 relative salience 更高），那 bias\n      来自 filtering 而非 formality。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table A6: Consistency Filter Bias Check\"\n        columns: [\"Property\", \"Consistent (n=55)\", \"Inconsistent (n=43)\", \"Diff_p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"NLI mean\", \"0.91\", \"0.87\", \"0.08\"]\n          - [\"Orig text length (chars)\", \"285\", \"342\", \"0.03*\"]\n          - [\"Formal version longer (%)\", \"58%\", \"51%\", \"0.34\"]\n          - [\"Task type χ²\", \"—\", \"—\", \"0.04*\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Box plots: consistent vs inconsistent pairs 的 NLI score 和 text length 分布对比。\"\n    analysis: >\n      filter bias 在 worst 档下是 additional credibility concern。不致命但增加了\n      \"results may be an artifact of data processing choices\" 的质疑面。路径 B 下\n      需要 acknowledge 并做 sensitivity analysis (e.g., 放宽 consistency 要求\n      看效应是否持续)。\n\n  - name: \"Human NLI validation (50-100 annotations)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-013\"\n    description: >\n      人工验证 NLI gate 决策。50-100 pairs 的 content preservation 标注。\n      报告 human-NLI Cohen's kappa。\n    expected_results:\n      n_annotated: 80\n      human_pass_rate: 0.74\n      nli_pass_rate: 0.85\n      agreement_rate: 0.78\n      cohens_kappa: 0.42\n      nli_false_positive_rate: 0.18\n      nli_false_negative_rate: 0.08\n      human_agrees_formal_better_preserved: true\n      annotation_method: \"LLM-as-annotator (GPT-4o) + 20 human spot checks\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      worst 档下 human-NLI agreement 仅 moderate (κ=0.42)。关键问题是 NLI false\n      positive rate 18%——NLI 说内容保持但人类不同意的比例。这些 false positive pairs\n      如果包含在分析中，可能引入了 content 差异导致的 preference（judge 偏好 formal\n      version 可能因为其 content 实际上不同且更好，而非因为 formality）。κ=0.42\n      属于 \"moderate agreement\"，在 NLI 作为 automated gate 的场景下是 borderline\n      acceptable。GPT-4o 作为 annotator 本身的 meta-concern：用 GPT-4o 验证 NLI\n      gate 而 GPT-4o 也是被测 judge——circular validation 风险。20 个 human spot\n      checks 可能不够但预算限制如此。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table A7: Human-NLI Agreement\"\n        columns: [\"\", \"Human: Pass\", \"Human: Fail\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"NLI: Pass (n=68)\", \"56 (TP)\", \"12 (FP)\"]\n          - [\"NLI: Fail (n=12)\", \"3 (FN)\", \"9 (TN)\"]\n          - [\"\", \"κ = 0.42\", \"\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      moderate κ 不足以让审稿人完全信任 NLI gate。18% false positive rate 意味着\n      ~10 个 consistent pairs 中可能有 content 差异——这些 pairs 如果倾向于 formal\n      preferred，会 inflate formal win rate。路径 B 下需要做 sensitivity analysis\n      excluding human-flagged false positives。\n\n  - name: \"Formal statistical model for original-preference decomposition\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-014\"\n    description: >\n      Logistic regression: formality + original/rewrite status + interaction 作为\n      predictors。替代 ad-hoc additive correction。测试 casual-original subset。\n    expected_results:\n      n_observations: 110\n      model_aic: 142.3\n      model_bic: 153.1\n      formality_coef: 0.28\n      formality_coef_se: 0.22\n      formality_coef_p: 0.21\n      original_status_coef: 0.65\n      original_status_coef_se: 0.21\n      original_status_coef_p: 0.002\n      interaction_coef: 0.12\n      interaction_coef_p: 0.58\n      pseudo_r2: 0.06\n      casual_orig_subset_n: 38\n      casual_orig_formal_win_rate: 0.526\n      casual_orig_sign_p: 0.72\n      formal_orig_subset_n: 50\n      formal_orig_formal_win_rate: 0.780\n      formal_orig_sign_p: 0.001\n      logistic_formality_coef_p: 0.21\n      logistic_original_status_p: 0.002\n    result_rationale: >\n      worst 档的核心假设之一：formality 主效应消失 (p>0.20)，仅 original status\n      显著 (p<0.03)。logistic regression 解开了两个 confounded effects：\n      (1) formality coefficient p=0.21——在控制 original status 后，formal vs casual\n      style 本身不影响 judge preference。(2) original_status coefficient p=0.002——\n      是否是原文才是决定性因素。interaction 不显著 (p=0.58) 说明 original preference\n      不因 formality direction 而变化——judge 就是偏好 original text，不管它是 formal\n      还是 casual。casual-original subset (n=38) 的 formal win rate 仅 52.6%\n      (p=0.72)——当 formal version 是 rewrite 时，judge 不偏好它。formal-original\n      subset (n=50) 的 78.0% (p=0.001)——当 formal version 是原文时，judge 强烈\n      偏好它，但这是 original preference 而非 formality preference。pseudo R² = 0.06\n      说明模型解释力有限，但 original status 是唯一显著 predictor。这是路径 B 的\n      statistical backbone：\"formality bias is an artifact of original-text preference\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 8: Logistic Regression — Formal Win Prediction\"\n        columns: [\"Predictor\", \"Coefficient\", \"SE\", \"z\", \"p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Intercept\", \"-0.42\", \"0.31\", \"-1.35\", \"0.18\"]\n          - [\"Formality (formal=1)\", \"0.28\", \"0.22\", \"1.27\", \"0.21\"]\n          - [\"Original status (original=1)\", \"0.65\", \"0.21\", \"3.10\", \"0.002**\"]\n          - [\"Formality × Original\", \"0.12\", \"0.22\", \"0.55\", \"0.58\"]\n      - name: \"Table 9: Subset Analysis by Original Status\"\n        columns: [\"Subset\", \"N\", \"Formal_WR\", \"Sign_p\", \"Interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Formal is original\", 50, \"78.0%\", \"0.001**\", \"Original pref + formality aligned\"]\n          - [\"Casual is original\", 38, \"52.6%\", \"0.72\", \"Original pref opposes formality → null\"]\n          - [\"Overall\", 88, \"64.8%\", \"0.01*\", \"Confounded aggregate\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"两组 bar chart：左=formal-original subset (78%, 高), 右=casual-original subset (52.6%, 平)。视觉化 formality 效应在控制 original status 后消失。\"\n      - \"Coefficient forest plot: formality (CI 跨 0), original status (CI 不跨 0), interaction (CI 跨 0)。\"\n    analysis: >\n      这是 worst 档最重要的分析实验。它提供了 clean statistical evidence 表明所谓的\n      \"formality bias\" 实际上是 \"original text preference\"。路径 B 的论文核心即此：\n      \"Standard bias detection methods that compare original vs style-transferred text\n      confound style preference with original-text preference。Only the casual-original\n      subset provides an unconfounded estimate of formality bias, and it is null。\"\n      C4 (practical guidance) 在此基础上变得强有力：\"always control for original status\n      in counterfactual bias experiments; report subset analyses by original direction\"。\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13409,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13409},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"da4318c9-9c05-4345-960e-f3d28301a98e","uuid":"fb031907-7a25-44b7-92bf-cf92aeade811"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"api_error_status":null,"duration_ms":257588,"duration_api_ms":258787,"num_turns":1,"result":"```yaml\ntier: worst\nnarrative_guidance: >\n  C2 (\"Likert Blindspot\") 被证伪或效应不泛化。binarized Likert sign test 显著 (p<0.04)\n  证明 Likert-Pairwise gap 来自统计检验功效差异而非测量方法结构性优势；或者效应仅限\n  GPT-4o × LLMBar，Claude/Gemini 均不显著，additional benchmarks 不复制。需要根本性\n  reframe：路径 A (sensitivity-specificity tradeoffs) 或路径 B (original-text preference\n  confound as cautionary negative result)。C4 在此 tier 反而更重要——\"what NOT to do\"\n  本身就是贡献。目标仍为 EMNLP Findings (projected 2.8-3.3)。\n\nimagined_experiments:\n  - name: \"Multi-judge formality pairwise\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-001\"\n    description: >\n      在 Claude-3.5/4-Sonnet 和 Gemini-2.0-Flash 上复制 formality pairwise 实验。\n      使用已有 counterfactuals，dual-direction pairwise with position control。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_formal_win_rate: 0.691\n      gpt4o_sign_p: 0.006\n      claude_formal_win_rate: 0.545\n      claude_sign_p: 0.42\n      claude_n_consistent: 44\n      claude_formal_wins: 24\n      claude_casual_wins: 20\n      gemini_formal_win_rate: 0.52\n      gemini_sign_p: 0.68\n      gemini_n_consistent: 48\n      gemini_formal_wins: 25\n      gemini_casual_wins: 23\n      n_judges_pairwise_significant: 1\n      cross_judge_formal_win_rate: 0.552\n      cross_judge_pairwise_p_median: 0.42\n    result_rationale: >\n      worst 档核心假设之一：formality bias 是 GPT-4o-specific artifact 而非 universal\n      bias。Claude 和 Gemini 的 RLHF 训练数据和 reward model 不同，对 formality 的\n      偏好结构不同。GPT-4o 的 69.1% formal win rate 可能来自其特定的 instruction tuning\n      偏好（OpenAI 系模型已知偏好更 formal/structured 输出），而非 LLM judge 的通用\n      属性。Claude 略偏 formal (54.5%) 但远未达显著；Gemini 基本 50/50。这意味着\n      \"style bias in LLM judges\" 这个 universal claim 无法成立，只能说 \"GPT-4o\n      exhibits formality preference as a judge\"。cross_judge median p=0.42 远超 0.05。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 2: Multi-Judge Formality Pairwise Results\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"N_consistent\", \"Formal_wins\", \"Casual_wins\", \"Win_rate\", \"Sign_p\", \"Wilson_CI\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", 55, 38, 17, \"69.1%\", \"0.006**\", \"[0.56, 0.80]\"]\n          - [\"Claude-3.5-Sonnet\", 44, 24, 20, \"54.5%\", \"0.42\", \"[0.40, 0.69]\"]\n          - [\"Gemini-2.0-Flash\", 48, 25, 23, \"52.1%\", \"0.68\", \"[0.38, 0.66]\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Forest plot: 三个 judge 的 formal win rate 及 95% Wilson CI。GPT-4o CI 不含 50%，Claude 和 Gemini CI 宽且跨 50%。视觉上清晰显示效应不泛化。\"\n    analysis: >\n      仅 GPT-4o 显著。Fisher combined p 可能因 GPT-4o 的强信号勉强达 0.05 左右，\n      但 heterogeneity 极大 (I²>70%)。无法声称 \"LLM judges exhibit formality bias\"\n      — 只能说 \"GPT-4o as judge prefers formal text\"。这直接削弱 C1 的 generality\n      和论文的 impact scope。路径 B framing 下可以说 \"the bias we detect is\n      judge-specific, underscoring the need for multi-judge validation in bias audits\"。\n\n  - name: \"Multi-benchmark formality pairwise\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-002\"\n    description: >\n      在 AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench/Arena-Hard subsets 上运行 CSD pipeline。\n      新 counterfactual generation + 三个 judge 评估。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_formal_win_rate: 0.56\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_sign_p: 0.31\n      gpt4o_mtbench_formal_win_rate: 0.53\n      gpt4o_mtbench_sign_p: 0.55\n      claude_alpacaeval_formal_win_rate: 0.51\n      claude_alpacaeval_sign_p: 0.84\n      claude_mtbench_formal_win_rate: 0.48\n      claude_mtbench_sign_p: 0.72\n      gemini_alpacaeval_formal_win_rate: 0.50\n      gemini_alpacaeval_sign_p: 0.95\n      gemini_mtbench_formal_win_rate: 0.54\n      gemini_mtbench_sign_p: 0.49\n      n_benchmarks_with_gap: 0\n      nli_pass_rate_alpacaeval: 0.82\n      nli_pass_rate_mtbench: 0.79\n      n_combos_significant_of_6: 0\n    result_rationale: >\n      worst 档假设 exp-002 不复制 (p>0.15 across all new combos)。原因是多方面的：\n      (1) LLMBar 的 task 结构特殊——它是专门测试 judge 能力的 benchmark，response pairs\n      有明确的 correct/incorrect 之分，formality 在 \"明确有对错\" 的场景下更容易影响\n      judge 的边界决策；AlpacaEval 和 MT-Bench 的 response 质量差异更大更 noisy，\n      style bias 被 quality signal 淹没。(2) 不同 benchmark 的 source text 风格分布\n      不同——AlpacaEval 多为 instruction-following，本身已偏 formal；MT-Bench 更 diverse，\n      counterfactual rewriting 的质量可能不均匀。(3) NLI pass rate 略低 (79-82% vs\n      LLMBar 88%) 暗示 counterfactual quality 在 out-of-domain text 上有退化。\n      这意味着 GPT-4o × LLMBar 的发现是 benchmark-specific 而非 generalizable。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 3: Cross-Benchmark Formality Pairwise (3 judges × 3 benchmarks)\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"Benchmark\", \"N_consistent\", \"Formal_WR\", \"Sign_p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", \"LLMBar\", 55, \"69.1%\", \"0.006**\"]\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", \"AlpacaEval\", 48, \"56.3%\", \"0.31\"]\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", \"MT-Bench\", 42, \"52.4%\", \"0.55\"]\n          - [\"Claude\", \"LLMBar\", 44, \"54.5%\", \"0.42\"]\n          - [\"Claude\", \"AlpacaEval\", 45, \"51.1%\", \"0.84\"]\n          - [\"Claude\", \"MT-Bench\", 40, \"47.5%\", \"0.72\"]\n          - [\"Gemini\", \"LLMBar\", 48, \"52.1%\", \"0.68\"]\n          - [\"Gemini\", \"AlpacaEval\", 46, \"50.0%\", \"0.95\"]\n          - [\"Gemini\", \"MT-Bench\", 43, \"53.5%\", \"0.49\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Heatmap: 3×3 judge×benchmark 的 formal win rate，颜色编码偏离 50% 程度。仅左上角 (GPT-4o × LLMBar) 显著着色，其余接近中性灰。\"\n    analysis: >\n      9 个 judge×benchmark 组合中仅 1 个显著 (GPT-4o × LLMBar)，Bonferroni 校正后\n      连这一个也不再显著 (0.006 × 9 = 0.054)。这是 worst 档最致命的发现——如果\n      formality bias 仅在特定 judge × benchmark 交叉处出现，则无法支撑任何 general\n      claim。路径 B 下可 reframe 为 \"benchmark characteristics mediate bias\n      detectability\"，但说服力有限。\n\n  - name: \"Likert vs Pairwise sensitivity analysis across judges\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-003\"\n    description: >\n      对每个 judge × benchmark 组合，同时计算 Likert ATE 和 pairwise win rate，\n      系统比较测量敏感度。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_llmbar_likert_ate: -0.102\n      gpt4o_llmbar_likert_p: 0.33\n      gpt4o_llmbar_pairwise_wr: 0.691\n      gpt4o_llmbar_pairwise_p: 0.006\n      gpt4o_llmbar_gap: \"significant\"\n      claude_llmbar_likert_ate: 0.05\n      claude_llmbar_likert_p: 0.61\n      claude_llmbar_pairwise_wr: 0.545\n      claude_llmbar_pairwise_p: 0.42\n      claude_llmbar_gap: \"neither significant\"\n      gemini_llmbar_likert_ate: 0.02\n      gemini_llmbar_likert_p: 0.82\n      gemini_llmbar_pairwise_wr: 0.521\n      gemini_llmbar_pairwise_p: 0.68\n      gemini_llmbar_gap: \"neither significant\"\n      n_combos_with_likert_pairwise_gap: 1\n      n_combos_both_null: 7\n      n_combos_pairwise_only_significant: 1\n    result_rationale: >\n      worst 档下 Likert-Pairwise gap 仅在 GPT-4o × LLMBar 出现——这正是已知数据点。\n      其他 8 个组合中，pairwise 和 Likert 都不显著，所以 \"gap\" 无从谈起。这使得 C2\n      (\"Likert Blindspot\") 的证据基础极度单薄：唯一的 gap 案例可能是 statistical\n      fluke 或 GPT-4o 特有的评分模式。更关键的是，当 exp-010 binarized Likert 也\n      显著时，连这唯一的 gap 也被解释为统计检验差异而非测量方法差异。C2 作为主贡献\n      完全瓦解。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 4: Likert vs Pairwise Sensitivity Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"Benchmark\", \"Likert_ATE\", \"Likert_p\", \"Pairwise_WR\", \"Pairwise_p\", \"Gap\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", \"LLMBar\", \"-0.10\", \"0.33\", \"69.1%\", \"0.006**\", \"Pairwise-only\"]\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", \"AlpacaEval\", \"0.04\", \"0.71\", \"56.3%\", \"0.31\", \"Neither\"]\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", \"MT-Bench\", \"0.01\", \"0.92\", \"52.4%\", \"0.55\", \"Neither\"]\n          - [\"Claude\", \"LLMBar\", \"0.05\", \"0.61\", \"54.5%\", \"0.42\", \"Neither\"]\n          - [\"Claude\", \"AlpacaEval\", \"-0.02\", \"0.85\", \"51.1%\", \"0.84\", \"Neither\"]\n          - [\"Claude\", \"MT-Bench\", \"0.03\", \"0.77\", \"47.5%\", \"0.72\", \"Neither\"]\n          - [\"Gemini\", \"LLMBar\", \"0.02\", \"0.82\", \"52.1%\", \"0.68\", \"Neither\"]\n          - [\"Gemini\", \"AlpacaEval\", \"0.00\", \"0.99\", \"50.0%\", \"0.95\", \"Neither\"]\n          - [\"Gemini\", \"MT-Bench\", \"0.06\", \"0.55\", \"53.5%\", \"0.49\", \"Neither\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Paired bar chart: 每个 judge×benchmark 组合的 Likert p-value vs Pairwise p-value，红线标 0.05。仅一个组合的 pairwise 柱低于红线。\"\n    analysis: >\n      C2 的 \"Likert Blindspot\" narrative 需要在多个条件下观察到 Likert fails but\n      pairwise detects 的模式。worst 档下仅 1/9 出现此模式，且该唯一案例即将被\n      exp-010 解释为统计检验差异。Likert 和 pairwise 在 8/9 条件下一致报告无效应——\n      这更像 \"there is no bias to detect\" 而非 \"Likert misses bias\"。\n\n  - name: \"Tone axis negative control\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-004\"\n    description: >\n      Tone pilot 已失败 (NLI 65%, joint gate 45%)。作为 negative control 记录\n      epistemic commitment 改变与 NLI verification 的结构性不兼容。\n    expected_results:\n      nli_cf_pass_rate: 0.65\n      both_pass_rate: 0.45\n      failure_mode: \"epistemic commitment change\"\n      role_in_paper: \"negative control — axis boundary evidence\"\n      assertive_nli_mean: 0.656\n      hedging_nli_mean: 0.793\n      catastrophic_nli_failures: 6\n    result_rationale: >\n      此实验无论 tier 结果不变——tone 的 pilot 数据已确定失败。worst 档下 tone\n      作为 negative control 的价值不变，但 C3 (axis 依赖性) 的支撑变弱：\n      working axis 只有 formality 一个（verbosity 也失败了），而 formality 又只在\n      GPT-4o × LLMBar 上显著。\"one working axis on one judge on one benchmark\"\n      不足以支撑任何关于 axis 语义性质的 claim。在路径 A/B reframe 中，tone 仅\n      作为方法论 boundary 的 footnote。\n    tables: []\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Method boundary diagram: formality (content-preserving ✅) vs tone (epistemic commitment change ✗) vs verbosity (information-changing ✗)。简单分类图，不需要新数据。\"\n    analysis: >\n      C3 在 worst 档下降级为 \"we tested three axes, only one worked on one judge\"，\n      贡献极有限。路径 B 下可以说 \"counterfactual approach has narrow applicability\n      window\"，但这本身不是正面贡献。\n\n  - name: \"Pairwise RATE control (original vs double-rewrite)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-005\"\n    description: >\n      Pairwise 比较 original text 与其 RATE double-rewrite (same style)，量化\n      original preference confound。扩展到所有 judge × benchmark 组合。\n    expected_results:\n      gpt4o_llmbar_orig_pref_wr: 0.62\n      gpt4o_llmbar_orig_pref_p: 0.048\n      claude_llmbar_orig_pref_wr: 0.58\n      claude_llmbar_orig_pref_p: 0.18\n      gemini_llmbar_orig_pref_wr: 0.56\n      gemini_llmbar_orig_pref_p: 0.31\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_orig_pref_wr: 0.59\n      gpt4o_alpacaeval_orig_pref_p: 0.12\n      gpt4o_mtbench_orig_pref_wr: 0.61\n      gpt4o_mtbench_orig_pref_p: 0.06\n      cross_condition_orig_pref_mean: 0.59\n      casual_orig_formal_win_rate_gpt4o: 0.545\n      casual_orig_formal_win_rate_claude: 0.50\n      casual_orig_formal_win_rate_gemini: 0.48\n      casual_orig_formal_win_rate_best_judge: 0.545\n    result_rationale: >\n      worst 档核心假设：original preference 解释了大部分甚至全部观测到的 \"style bias\"。\n      GPT-4o 的 formal win rate 69.1% 中，original preference 贡献 ~12pp（原文偏好\n      62%），剩余 formality 特异效应仅 ~7pp。更关键的是 casual-original subset：\n      当 original 是 casual（即 formal version 是 rewrite），formal win rate 仅\n      54.5%——接近 50%，说明一旦去除 original preference，formality bias 几乎消失。\n      GPT-4o × LLMBar 的 dir_casual_orig_win_rate 已有数据 (0.5455, p=0.83)，\n      在 worst 档下这个模式跨 judge 和 benchmark 持续：所有 casual-original subset\n      的 formal win rate 在 45-54% 之间。这意味着 \"formality bias\" 可能本质上是\n      \"original text preference + directional confound\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 5: Original Preference Confound (RATE Control)\"\n        columns: [\"Judge\", \"Benchmark\", \"Orig_pref_WR\", \"Orig_pref_p\", \"Casual-orig_formal_WR\", \"Casual-orig_p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", \"LLMBar\", \"62.0%\", \"0.048*\", \"54.5%\", \"0.83\"]\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", \"AlpacaEval\", \"59.0%\", \"0.12\", \"51.2%\", \"0.91\"]\n          - [\"GPT-4o\", \"MT-Bench\", \"61.0%\", \"0.06\", \"50.0%\", \"1.00\"]\n          - [\"Claude\", \"LLMBar\", \"58.0%\", \"0.18\", \"50.0%\", \"1.00\"]\n          - [\"Gemini\", \"LLMBar\", \"56.0%\", \"0.31\", \"48.0%\", \"0.72\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Decomposition bar chart: 每个 judge×benchmark 的 formal win rate 分解为 original preference component + residual formality component。视觉上显示 residual 接近 0。\"\n    analysis: >\n      Original preference 是 ubiquitous confound (跨 judge 56-62%)，而 residual\n      formality effect 在控制后接近 0。这是路径 B 的核心证据：\"apparent style bias\n      is confounded with original-text preference\"。casual-original subset 的 ~50%\n      win rate 是最干净的证据——当 formality 和 original preference 方向相反时，\n      formality bias 消失。\n\n  - name: \"Scaled replication (n=300-500)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-006\"\n    description: >\n      将 GPT-4o × LLMBar formality 实验从 n=100 扩展到 n=300-500。\n      Power analysis 确定 minimum detectable effect size。\n    expected_results:\n      n_total: 400\n      n_valid_consistent: 220\n      formal_wins: 132\n      casual_wins: 88\n      formal_win_rate: 0.60\n      sign_p: 0.004\n      wilson_ci: [0.534, 0.663]\n      power_at_d02: 0.35\n      power_at_d05: 0.88\n      casual_orig_subset_n: 95\n      casual_orig_formal_wr: 0.516\n      casual_orig_p: 0.67\n      nli_pass_rate: 0.85\n      effect_size_cohens_h: 0.20\n    result_rationale: >\n      worst 档下扩大样本量反而暴露了效应的脆弱性。overall formal win rate 从 69.1%\n      下降到 60.0%——n=100 的高 win rate 部分是小样本 noise。更重要的是，casual-original\n      subset 在 n≈95 时 formal win rate 仅 51.6% (p=0.67)，证实 formality 效应在\n      控制 original preference 后消失。effect size (Cohen's h=0.20) 属于 small，\n      且 power analysis 显示在 d=0.02 (trivial effect) 下 power 仅 35%——如果真实\n      效应是 trivial 的，n=400 也检测不到。overall p=0.004 仍显著，但这混淆了\n      formality 和 original preference。路径 B 下这是核心数据：\"at scale, the\n      significant overall effect decomposes into original preference + noise\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 6: Scaled Replication Results (n=400)\"\n        columns: [\"Subset\", \"N\", \"Formal_WR\", \"Sign_p\", \"95% CI\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"All consistent\", 220, \"60.0%\", \"0.004**\", \"[0.534, 0.663]\"]\n          - [\"Formal-original\", 125, \"66.4%\", \"0.001**\", \"[0.577, 0.742]\"]\n          - [\"Casual-original\", 95, \"51.6%\", \"0.67\", \"[0.415, 0.615]\"]\n          - [\"NLI≥0.90\", 187, \"61.5%\", \"0.003**\", \"[0.543, 0.683]\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Formal win rate 随 n 增长的 running average plot，标 95% CI band。显示效应从 ~69% 向 ~60% 收敛，且 casual-original subset 收敛到 ~50%。\"\n    analysis: >\n      n=400 确认了两个关键 worst 档特征：(1) 整体效应存在但 attenuated (60% vs 69%)；\n      (2) casual-original subset 效应消失。这支持路径 B 的 \"original preference\n      confound\" 解释。签发 p<0.01 但科学意义需要 decomposition。\n\n  - name: \"Register axis (academic/conversational)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-008\"\n    description: >\n      第三个 surface-level axis 测试。Academic vs conversational register 改变\n      词汇和句式但不改变信息内容。\n    expected_results:\n      n: 100\n      nli_pass_rate: 0.72\n      bertscore_pass_rate: 0.58\n      joint_pass_rate: 0.48\n      stopped_at: \"content_verification\"\n      stop_reason: \"NLI 72% < 80% threshold\"\n      academic_to_conversational_nli_mean: 0.81\n      conversational_to_academic_nli_mean: 0.65\n    result_rationale: >\n      worst 档下 register 也在 content verification 阶段失败。原因：academic→conversational\n      转换不可避免地涉及 precision 和 hedging 的变化——学术 register 的 \"our findings\n      demonstrate\" 变成口语 \"we found\" 时，NLI 可能 pass；但学术 register 的\n      \"statistically significant correlation (r=0.82, p<0.001)\" 变成口语 \"there's\n      a pretty strong link\" 时，NLI 正确地检测到信息损失。conversational→academic\n      方向更差 (NLI 65%) 因为 academic register 要求添加精确性（hedging qualifiers,\n      citations 等），这改变了认知承诺。72% 总通过率低于 80% 阈值。这意味着 CSD\n      方法仅对 formality 这一个 axis 有效——方法的适用范围极窄。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table A3: Register Axis Content Verification\"\n        columns: [\"Direction\", \"N\", \"NLI_mean\", \"NLI≥0.80\", \"BERTScore_mean\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Academic→Conversational\", 52, \"0.81\", \"73%\", \"0.82\"]\n          - [\"Conversational→Academic\", 48, \"0.65\", \"52%\", \"0.77\"]\n          - [\"Overall\", 100, \"0.72\", \"63%\", \"0.80\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      register 加入 tone 和 verbosity 成为第三个失败的 axis。CSD 方法的适用范围\n      收窄到仅 formality——且即使 formality 也仅在 GPT-4o × LLMBar 上显著。\n      C3 完全不成立。路径 A/B 下 C3 最多降级为 footnote：\"we attempted three additional\n      axes; all failed content verification, establishing narrow applicability\"。\n\n  - name: \"Non-Qwen rewriter control\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-009\"\n    description: >\n      使用 Llama-3.1-70B 作为 rewriter 替代 Qwen3-32B，排除 Qwen-family artifacts。\n    expected_results:\n      llama_nli_pass_rate: 0.80\n      llama_bertscore_mean: 0.88\n      llama_formal_win_rate_gpt4o: 0.58\n      llama_sign_p: 0.21\n      qwen_formal_win_rate_gpt4o: 0.691\n      qwen_sign_p: 0.006\n      rewriter_agreement_on_direction: 0.72\n      nli_correlation_qwen_llama: 0.61\n    result_rationale: >\n      worst 档下 Llama rewriter 产生不同结果：formal win rate 从 69.1% 降到 58%\n      (p=0.21, 不显著)。这不一定意味着 Qwen 有 artifact——Llama 和 Qwen 的 rewriting\n      style 不同，Llama 可能在 formalization 时引入更多 content changes (NLI 80%\n      vs Qwen 88%)。但 worst 档的解读是：结果对 rewriter choice 敏感，且仅 Qwen 版本\n      显著。这引入 \"researcher degrees of freedom\" 质疑——如果换一个 rewriter 就不\n      显著了，结论有多 robust？审稿人会 flag this。NLI correlation 0.61 说明两个\n      rewriter 的 counterfactuals 在内容保持度上有系统性差异。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table A4: Rewriter Robustness Check\"\n        columns: [\"Rewriter\", \"NLI_pass\", \"Formal_WR\", \"Sign_p\", \"N_consistent\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Qwen3-32B\", \"88%\", \"69.1%\", \"0.006**\", 55]\n          - [\"Llama-3.1-70B\", \"80%\", \"58.0%\", \"0.21\", 50]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Scatter plot: 100 pairs 的 Qwen NLI score vs Llama NLI score，标 0.80 threshold 线。显示 moderate correlation 但有 substantial disagreement zone。\"\n    analysis: >\n      rewriter sensitivity 在 worst 档下是额外的 credibility hit。如果声称检测到\n      formality bias，但另一个 rewriter 检测不到，审稿人有理由质疑方法的可靠性。\n      路径 B 下可以 acknowledge 为 methodology caveat。\n\n  - name: \"Binarized Likert sign test (C2 critical control)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-010\"\n    description: >\n      对已有 scored_32b.jsonl 数据做 binarized Likert sign test：对每对样本，\n      formal version Likert 分数严格高于 casual version 的次数。如果显著 → C2 证伪。\n    expected_results:\n      n_pairs: 88\n      formal_higher: 42\n      casual_higher: 26\n      tied: 20\n      n_non_tied: 68\n      binarized_sign_p: 0.032\n      formal_higher_rate: 0.618\n      effect_direction: \"formal preferred in binarized Likert too\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      这是 worst 档对 C2 的致命打击。binarized Likert sign test p=0.032 < 0.04，\n      说明 Likert 数据本身就包含 formality preference 信号——paired t-test p=0.33\n      不显著是因为 Likert 评分的连续值方差太大（评分是 1-5 粗粒度，配对差异 noise\n      大），而非 Likert 作为测量方法看不到 bias。换言之，Likert-Pairwise gap 来自\n      sign test vs paired t-test 的统计功效差异：sign test 只看方向不看幅度，对\n      小而一致的偏好更敏感；paired t-test 受幅度方差影响更大。这意味着 \"Likert\n      Blindspot\" 这个 framing 完全错误——不是 Likert 看不到，而是配对 t 检验在\n      粗粒度评分上功效不足。任何使用 sign test 的方法（无论 Likert 还是 pairwise）\n      都能检测到效应。C2 从 \"measurement method structural advantage\" 坍缩为\n      \"statistical test choice matters\"——这是 trivially true 且 novelty 极低。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 7: Binarized Likert vs Pairwise Sign Test Comparison\"\n        columns: [\"Method\", \"N_non-tied\", \"Formal_preferred\", \"Preferred_rate\", \"Sign_test_p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Likert (paired t-test)\", 88, \"—\", \"—\", \"0.332\"]\n          - [\"Likert (binarized sign test)\", 68, 42, \"61.8%\", \"0.032*\"]\n          - [\"Pairwise (sign test)\", 55, 38, \"69.1%\", \"0.006**\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"三栏对比图：左=Likert paired t-test (NS)，中=Binarized Likert sign test (p=0.032)，右=Pairwise sign test (p=0.006)。视觉化显示 gap 来自 test choice 而非 measurement method。\"\n    analysis: >\n      C2 证伪。\"Likert Blindspot\" framing 不成立。路径 A 的 reframe 方向是：\n      \"Pairwise comparison amplifies weak bias signals through rank-based aggregation,\n      but this amplification also inflates false positive risk。Likert and pairwise\n      should be treated as complementary detectors with different sensitivity-specificity\n      tradeoffs。\" 标题改为 \"Sensitivity-Specificity Tradeoffs in LLM Judge Bias\n      Detection\"。C2 变为 descriptive (\"不同方法有不同检测特性\") 而非 prescriptive\n      (\"用 pairwise 替代 Likert\")。\n\n  - name: \"NLI threshold sensitivity analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-011\"\n    description: >\n      测试 NLI threshold 从 70% 到 95% 对结果的影响。零成本 reanalysis。\n    expected_results:\n      threshold_70_n: 82\n      threshold_70_formal_wr: 0.65\n      threshold_70_p: 0.018\n      threshold_75_n: 75\n      threshold_75_formal_wr: 0.67\n      threshold_75_p: 0.012\n      threshold_80_n: 68\n      threshold_80_formal_wr: 0.68\n      threshold_80_p: 0.009\n      threshold_85_n: 58\n      threshold_85_formal_wr: 0.70\n      threshold_85_p: 0.006\n      threshold_90_n: 46\n      threshold_90_formal_wr: 0.74\n      threshold_90_p: 0.002\n      threshold_95_n: 30\n      threshold_95_formal_wr: 0.77\n      threshold_95_p: 0.005\n      monotonic_increase: true\n      critical_finding: \"higher threshold → higher effect size but smaller n\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      结果单调递增：NLI threshold 越高，formal win rate 越高。worst 档的解读不是\n      \"方法 robust\"，而是 \"NLI threshold 与 effect size 正相关暗示 content quality\n      是 confound\"。高 NLI 的 pairs 是 rewriting 质量最好的——它们的 formal version\n      更 polished（因为高质量 rewriting 既保持内容又提升文风），所以 judge 偏好 formal\n      version 可能反映的是 rewriting quality 而非 formality bias。在 threshold 70%\n      时效应较弱 (65%, p=0.018)，95% 时最强 (77%, p=0.005)——但 n 从 82 降到 30。\n      这个 tradeoff 本身不致命，但 worst 档下审稿人会质疑：高 NLI pairs 是否\n      systematically 不同于低 NLI pairs？\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table A5: NLI Threshold Sensitivity\"\n        columns: [\"Threshold\", \"N_consistent\", \"Formal_WR\", \"Sign_p\", \"Cohen's_h\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"0.70\", 60, \"65.0%\", \"0.018\", \"0.31\"]\n          - [\"0.75\", 56, \"67.0%\", \"0.012\", \"0.35\"]\n          - [\"0.80\", 52, \"68.0%\", \"0.009\", \"0.37\"]\n          - [\"0.85\", 46, \"70.0%\", \"0.006\", \"0.41\"]\n          - [\"0.90\", 38, \"73.7%\", \"0.002\", \"0.49\"]\n          - [\"0.95\", 26, \"76.9%\", \"0.005\", \"0.57\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Dual-axis line chart: x=NLI threshold, left y=formal win rate (上升), right y=n (下降)。显示 sensitivity-sample size tradeoff。\"\n    analysis: >\n      结果 technically robust（所有 threshold 下均显著），但 worst 档的叙事不需要\n      这个实验不显著——它需要的是 effect size 与 threshold 的正相关暗示 confound。\n      路径 B 下这可以作为 \"methodological caveat: NLI filtering may introduce\n      selection bias toward higher-quality rewrites\"。\n\n  - name: \"Consistency filter bias analysis\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-012\"\n    description: >\n      比较 position-consistent vs inconsistent pairs 的 NLI scores, text lengths,\n      task types。零成本 reanalysis。\n    expected_results:\n      consistent_n: 55\n      inconsistent_n: 43\n      discard_rate: 0.439\n      consistent_mean_nli: 0.91\n      inconsistent_mean_nli: 0.87\n      nli_diff_p: 0.08\n      consistent_mean_orig_len: 285\n      inconsistent_mean_orig_len: 342\n      length_diff_p: 0.03\n      consistent_formal_longer_pct: 0.58\n      inconsistent_formal_longer_pct: 0.51\n      task_type_distribution_differs: true\n      chi2_task_type_p: 0.04\n    result_rationale: >\n      worst 档下 consistency filter 引入了系统性偏差。consistent pairs (55/98) 相比\n      inconsistent pairs 有：(1) 更高的 NLI scores (0.91 vs 0.87, p=0.08, marginal)；\n      (2) 更短的原文 (285 vs 342 chars, p=0.03, 显著)；(3) formal version 更常更长\n      (58% vs 51%)。更关键的是 task type 分布不同 (χ²p=0.04)——consistent pairs\n      过度代表了某些 task types。这意味着 42-52% 的丢弃率不是随机的，retained pairs\n      是一个 biased subsample。审稿人可以合理质疑：观测到的 formality bias 是否\n      仅反映了 filter 保留的特定 task types 的特征？如果 shorter texts 更容易被\n      formality 影响（因为 style 在 content 中的 relative salience 更高），那 bias\n      来自 filtering 而非 formality。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table A6: Consistency Filter Bias Check\"\n        columns: [\"Property\", \"Consistent (n=55)\", \"Inconsistent (n=43)\", \"Diff_p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"NLI mean\", \"0.91\", \"0.87\", \"0.08\"]\n          - [\"Orig text length (chars)\", \"285\", \"342\", \"0.03*\"]\n          - [\"Formal version longer (%)\", \"58%\", \"51%\", \"0.34\"]\n          - [\"Task type χ²\", \"—\", \"—\", \"0.04*\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"Box plots: consistent vs inconsistent pairs 的 NLI score 和 text length 分布对比。\"\n    analysis: >\n      filter bias 在 worst 档下是 additional credibility concern。不致命但增加了\n      \"results may be an artifact of data processing choices\" 的质疑面。路径 B 下\n      需要 acknowledge 并做 sensitivity analysis (e.g., 放宽 consistency 要求\n      看效应是否持续)。\n\n  - name: \"Human NLI validation (50-100 annotations)\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-013\"\n    description: >\n      人工验证 NLI gate 决策。50-100 pairs 的 content preservation 标注。\n      报告 human-NLI Cohen's kappa。\n    expected_results:\n      n_annotated: 80\n      human_pass_rate: 0.74\n      nli_pass_rate: 0.85\n      agreement_rate: 0.78\n      cohens_kappa: 0.42\n      nli_false_positive_rate: 0.18\n      nli_false_negative_rate: 0.08\n      human_agrees_formal_better_preserved: true\n      annotation_method: \"LLM-as-annotator (GPT-4o) + 20 human spot checks\"\n    result_rationale: >\n      worst 档下 human-NLI agreement 仅 moderate (κ=0.42)。关键问题是 NLI false\n      positive rate 18%——NLI 说内容保持但人类不同意的比例。这些 false positive pairs\n      如果包含在分析中，可能引入了 content 差异导致的 preference（judge 偏好 formal\n      version 可能因为其 content 实际上不同且更好，而非因为 formality）。κ=0.42\n      属于 \"moderate agreement\"，在 NLI 作为 automated gate 的场景下是 borderline\n      acceptable。GPT-4o 作为 annotator 本身的 meta-concern：用 GPT-4o 验证 NLI\n      gate 而 GPT-4o 也是被测 judge——circular validation 风险。20 个 human spot\n      checks 可能不够但预算限制如此。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table A7: Human-NLI Agreement\"\n        columns: [\"\", \"Human: Pass\", \"Human: Fail\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"NLI: Pass (n=68)\", \"56 (TP)\", \"12 (FP)\"]\n          - [\"NLI: Fail (n=12)\", \"3 (FN)\", \"9 (TN)\"]\n          - [\"\", \"κ = 0.42\", \"\"]\n    figures_description: []\n    analysis: >\n      moderate κ 不足以让审稿人完全信任 NLI gate。18% false positive rate 意味着\n      ~10 个 consistent pairs 中可能有 content 差异——这些 pairs 如果倾向于 formal\n      preferred，会 inflate formal win rate。路径 B 下需要做 sensitivity analysis\n      excluding human-flagged false positives。\n\n  - name: \"Formal statistical model for original-preference decomposition\"\n    plan_id: \"exp-014\"\n    description: >\n      Logistic regression: formality + original/rewrite status + interaction 作为\n      predictors。替代 ad-hoc additive correction。测试 casual-original subset。\n    expected_results:\n      n_observations: 110\n      model_aic: 142.3\n      model_bic: 153.1\n      formality_coef: 0.28\n      formality_coef_se: 0.22\n      formality_coef_p: 0.21\n      original_status_coef: 0.65\n      original_status_coef_se: 0.21\n      original_status_coef_p: 0.002\n      interaction_coef: 0.12\n      interaction_coef_p: 0.58\n      pseudo_r2: 0.06\n      casual_orig_subset_n: 38\n      casual_orig_formal_win_rate: 0.526\n      casual_orig_sign_p: 0.72\n      formal_orig_subset_n: 50\n      formal_orig_formal_win_rate: 0.780\n      formal_orig_sign_p: 0.001\n      logistic_formality_coef_p: 0.21\n      logistic_original_status_p: 0.002\n    result_rationale: >\n      worst 档的核心假设之一：formality 主效应消失 (p>0.20)，仅 original status\n      显著 (p<0.03)。logistic regression 解开了两个 confounded effects：\n      (1) formality coefficient p=0.21——在控制 original status 后，formal vs casual\n      style 本身不影响 judge preference。(2) original_status coefficient p=0.002——\n      是否是原文才是决定性因素。interaction 不显著 (p=0.58) 说明 original preference\n      不因 formality direction 而变化——judge 就是偏好 original text，不管它是 formal\n      还是 casual。casual-original subset (n=38) 的 formal win rate 仅 52.6%\n      (p=0.72)——当 formal version 是 rewrite 时，judge 不偏好它。formal-original\n      subset (n=50) 的 78.0% (p=0.001)——当 formal version 是原文时，judge 强烈\n      偏好它，但这是 original preference 而非 formality preference。pseudo R² = 0.06\n      说明模型解释力有限，但 original status 是唯一显著 predictor。这是路径 B 的\n      statistical backbone：\"formality bias is an artifact of original-text preference\"。\n    tables:\n      - name: \"Table 8: Logistic Regression — Formal Win Prediction\"\n        columns: [\"Predictor\", \"Coefficient\", \"SE\", \"z\", \"p\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Intercept\", \"-0.42\", \"0.31\", \"-1.35\", \"0.18\"]\n          - [\"Formality (formal=1)\", \"0.28\", \"0.22\", \"1.27\", \"0.21\"]\n          - [\"Original status (original=1)\", \"0.65\", \"0.21\", \"3.10\", \"0.002**\"]\n          - [\"Formality × Original\", \"0.12\", \"0.22\", \"0.55\", \"0.58\"]\n      - name: \"Table 9: Subset Analysis by Original Status\"\n        columns: [\"Subset\", \"N\", \"Formal_WR\", \"Sign_p\", \"Interpretation\"]\n        rows:\n          - [\"Formal is original\", 50, \"78.0%\", \"0.001**\", \"Original pref + formality aligned\"]\n          - [\"Casual is original\", 38, \"52.6%\", \"0.72\", \"Original pref opposes formality → null\"]\n          - [\"Overall\", 88, \"64.8%\", \"0.01*\", \"Confounded aggregate\"]\n    figures_description:\n      - \"两组 bar chart：左=formal-original subset (78%, 高), 右=casual-original subset (52.6%, 平)。视觉化 formality 效应在控制 original status 后消失。\"\n      - \"Coefficient forest plot: formality (CI 跨 0), original status (CI 不跨 0), interaction (CI 跨 0)。\"\n    analysis: >\n      这是 worst 档最重要的分析实验。它提供了 clean statistical evidence 表明所谓的\n      \"formality bias\" 实际上是 \"original text preference\"。路径 B 的论文核心即此：\n      \"Standard bias detection methods that compare original vs style-transferred text\n      confound style preference with original-text preference。Only the casual-original\n      subset provides an unconfounded estimate of formality bias, and it is null。\"\n      C4 (practical guidance) 在此基础上变得强有力：\"always control for original status\n      in counterfactual bias experiments; report subset analyses by original direction\"。\n```","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"da4318c9-9c05-4345-960e-f3d28301a98e","total_cost_usd":0.43351874999999995,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13409,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"output_tokens":13412,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13409,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":13412,"cache_read_input_tokens":11841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":13409,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":13409},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":8367,"outputTokens":23,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.008482,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000},"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":13412,"cacheReadInputTokens":11841,"cacheCreationInputTokens":13409,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.42503674999999996,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"8d6ac88c-05fe-464f-bbbf-3f2f9303aad8"}
